---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/EditorialNav.astro';
import '../styles/editorial.css';
import data from '../../public/avg-rent.json';
const cities = data.flatMap(entry => entry.cities.filter(city => !city.retired && !city.unavailable));
const pairs = new Set(data.flatMap(entry => entry.cities.filter(city => !city.retired && !city.unavailable).map(city => entry.country + '/' + city.city)));
const anomalies = cities.filter(c => (typeof c.rent1 === 'number' && typeof c.rent2 === 'number' && c.rent2 < c.rent1) || (typeof c.rent2 === 'number' && typeof c.rent3 === 'number' && c.rent3 < c.rent2)).length;
---
<Layout title="About RentMap — data sources, calculations and limitations" description="Understand the difference between RentMap's stored rent snapshot, listing map and official rent index, including missing dates and calculation methods." canonical="https://rentmap.net/about/">
<main class="editorial"><Nav /><header><p class="eyebrow">Our data, explained</p><h1>Useful comparisons start with honest limitations.</h1><p class="intro">RentMap is an independent rental research tool. We help you compare figures and ask better questions before choosing a home. We do not act as a landlord, broker or rental agency.</p><p class="small">Rent snapshot retrieved 28 September 2026; source table last updated September 2026. Per-city observation dates and sample counts were not provided.</p></header>
<section class="panel"><h2>Three different kinds of information</h2><h3>1. The stored city snapshot</h3><p>The country and city pages read {cities.length} active records across {data.length} countries, representing {pairs.size} distinct city-country pairs. We matched each active country/city and its bedroom values to the expanded <a href="https://www.globalpropertyguide.com/property-rent-prices-by-country" rel="nofollow">Global Property Guide rent table</a>. Values retain the source's displayed EUR or USD currency. Explicit “n.a.” cells remain unavailable. Wellington and Chon Buri are retired because they do not appear in the captured table.</p><p>The source identifies the table update month but does not provide per-city observation dates or sample sizes in this capture. Reuse permission/terms have not been established; attribution is not a license. These figures are snapshots, not current rental offers or guarantees of today's market.</p><p>The combined value is our arithmetic mean of the available bedroom-size values, not a median of homes or local advertisements. The source describes its bedroom prices as median monthly asking rents; our combined figure is a separate calculation.</p><h3>2. Individual listings on the map</h3><p>The map uses a separate listing feed with property details and original source links where supplied. These listings are not the input to the country and city snapshot figures. A map marker is a lead to investigate, not confirmation that a home is available. Locations may be approximate, and coverage differs between markets.</p><h3>3. Official Danish rent indices</h3><p>Statistics Denmark publishes HUS1 rent indices by region and housing type. The published table now uses a different base period than the one in our stored extract; we have removed the stale values and link directly to the <a href="https://m.statbank.dk/TableInfo/HUS1?lang=en">current official HUS1 table</a>. Indices measure change relative to a base period, not rent amounts, and regional indices are not city-specific asking-rent estimates.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>What our calculations mean</h2><ul><li><strong>Combined city reference:</strong> rounded arithmetic mean of available one-, two- and three-bedroom figures. Each available home size gets equal weight, not weight by number of listings.</li><li><strong>Country reference:</strong> arithmetic mean of active city combined figures. Each record receives equal weight; this is not a population-weighted national rent estimate. Missing and retired cities are not assigned zero.</li><li><strong>Weekly equivalent:</strong> monthly figure × 12 ÷ 52, rounded to a whole unit of the displayed currency.</li><li><strong>Rankings:</strong> ordering the available snapshot records by their combined figure. Our lists do not cover every city, measure local purchasing power or establish a good place to live.</li><li><strong>Budget tool:</strong> calculations use only the numbers you enter. No city snapshot or listing price is silently substituted into your budget.</li></ul><p>The captured source marks some bedroom values “n.a.”; those cells are kept unavailable and omitted from the combined mean. The dataset contains {anomalies} records where a larger bedroom category is cheaper than the preceding one. Different samples can produce that pattern, but the capture does not expose underlying samples needed to determine why.</p></section>
<section><h2>How to use the information responsibly</h2><p>Begin with the bedroom category that matches your search. Check several original advertisements in the same neighbourhood, for the same rental period, furnishing and included costs. A snapshot can suggest what to investigate, but an actual budget needs a current price and a confirmed list of charges.</p><p>Do not infer a city's safety, legal requirements, internet reliability or job market from its rent. Use relevant official sources for those questions. If a market is missing from our map or dataset, we do not know its rent from this data.</p></section>
<section class="panel tint"><h2>Editorial responsibility and corrections</h2><p>RentMap publishes the explanations, calculation tools and comparisons on this site. Our editorial standard is to distinguish stored reference figures, live listing records and hypothetical examples; avoid unsupported freshness claims; and expose the assumptions behind calculations.</p><p>Send corrections to <a href="mailto:kontakt@lejel.dk">kontakt@lejel.dk</a> with the RentMap page, the value or statement in question, a public source URL and its date. Do not send identity documents or private tenancy records. We can review a reported discrepancy against its source before changing a stored value.</p><p>Advertising scripts are currently disabled. Ownership verification does not mean that ads are being served or that Google has approved the site.</p></section>
</main></Layout>
